      "mergeID": "66b2a8b1e43101e40136bc9e",
      "mergedPostDetails": "With Index controllers, I've found that it's much harder to curl my fingers smoothly compared to Live, especially the middle/ring/pinky fingers. I practically have to grip the controller to get those fingers to curl, and the finger kind of jerks from straightened to bent.\n\nOn Live, it's a lot smoother and I can see my avatar fingers smoothly curl continuously while curling my fingers.\n\nVirtual Desktop 1.32.10 beta\n\nQuest Pro w/ Index Controllers",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1481] Harder to curl fingers smoothly with Index controllers",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "66ac37dcd0a0bcd3ed895155",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "1484 update: the \"Legacy Fingers\" toggle doesn't appear to help with this at all. Either way, curling is still jank. I forgot to test the \"Avatars Use Finger Tracking\" toggle, but that one may be it",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
