      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "\"Legacy Fingers\" in the beta have a number of discrepancies with the \"full grip\", it does not work at all on the left hand and requires trigger pull with the right hand (trigger pull on the right hand will turn on the more \"aggressive\" curl for any finger on the grip).\n\nOn live \"full grip\" is achieved entirely by the grip, sometimes requiring a small bit of force to actuate (this happens to me somewhat exclusively with my right controller, wasn't always the case, however I'm not sure if that's due to aged hardware or a change that happened in VRChat within the past year or so) and usually 2 or more fingers on the grip, the trigger and/or thumb inputs have no impact whatsoever.\n\nLive: https://youtu.be/LlXQVgA2ij0\n\nBeta: https://youtu.be/NT6Q8VBJFao\n\nAnother discrepancy of \"Legacy Fingers\" is that with the dashboard open the hand gesture will be the \"claw\" instead of \"open hand\", however I did not include that in the video. EDIT: Canny - https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/locking-gestures-with-legacy-fingers-affects-hand-pose-while-in-the-steamvr-dash",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
