      "mergeID": "66ad3d9ac8a0f0464ea76f48",
      "mergedPostDetails": "A lot of VRChat players prefer to use legacy finger tracking there is a reason the feature was requested, as the new splay added to the finger tracking looks awful on many models, the index doesn't have splay floats so artificially adding them looks very unnatural to a lot of players. Ive gone ahead and created two videos from Live 1472 and Beta 1485 and these are not at all comparable, this is more like legacy + removed tracking points.\n\nOpen Beta 1485: https://youtu.be/GVV9QtsY0B0\n\nyou can no longer properly close your hands and now thumb tracking has gone completely.\n\nLive 1472: https://youtu.be/_caGQNvgi5o\n\nLive looks an immeasurable amount better than open beta legacy finger tracking with hands properly closing and thumbs being tracks on all 6 points on the controller (A button, B Button, Track Pad top and bottom, system button and the thumb-stick sensor.\n\nPlease implement the original finger tracking for index that is currently in live build 1472, what we have currently in Open Beta 1485 with legacy tracking enabled is a immeasurable downgrade.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1485] Open Beta legacy finger tracking is a awful downgrade",
